# gate/vocabulary.admitted — the admitted public native vocabulary of Idol.
#
# DENY BY DEFAULT. A public module-scope identity -- relation, descriptor,
# case, or binding -- that is not spelled here is not admitted, and a diff
# that introduces one is rejected. That is the whole mechanism.
#
# WHY IT IS A LIST AND NOT A HEURISTIC. A mashed compound like
# `rolebeginexpr`, or a `call_extern` quietly renamed to `callextern`, is not
# stopped here because a checker judged its morphology. Nothing in this gate
# knows what a good name looks like, and nothing in it must ever learn: shape
# rules are exactly the kind of judgement a high-throughput text generator
# talks itself past. It is stopped because THE WORD IS NOT ON THIS LIST.
#
# HOW TO ADD A WORD. Add the line. That edit is the audit trail, and it is
# the point: naming a new public identity becomes a visible, reviewable act
# instead of a side effect of a large patch.
#
# PROVENANCE. Seeded 2026-08-22 from idol@40de041c by
# gate/vocab-extract.awk -- the same program gate/vocabulary.sh checks with,
# so there is no drift between how a word got admitted and how it is tested.
#   subjects .............. 1010 tracked .id files
#   declarations found .... 7875 public module-scope declarations
#   distinct words ........ 5033
# The seed is today's vocabulary, debt included. It is not an endorsement of
# every word on it. Its job is to make word 5034 require a human.
